# {{PROJECT_NAME}}

This application was created from the deterministic Vellum `basic` template.
Application behavior belongs in `src/`; generated design material belongs in
`ui/generated/` and should not be hand-edited.

```sh
vellum doctor --fix --require-target macos
vellum build --target macos
vellum dev --target macos
vellum test --target macos
vellum run --target macos
vellum capture --scenario smoke --output artifacts/smoke.png
vellum capture --matrix tests/capture-matrix.json --montage --output artifacts/montage.png
vellum package --target macos --output dist
```

The optional browser lane requires Chrome:

```sh
vellum build --target web
vellum dev --target web
vellum test --target web
vellum run --target web
vellum package --target web --output dist-web
```

`run --target web` returns the exact finite local-server command for the static
build; it does not leave a hidden background process.

`dev` owns an interactive watch/rebuild/reload session and writes a versioned
transcript under `.vellum/state/`. Native reload is a process restart (with
continuity only for explicit `persistence = "state-v1"`); web reload is a
full-page reload and currently resets in-memory state.

`app.toml` is the sole editable application, target, capability, and packaging
manifest. `framework.lock` pins the exact SDK artifact and JavaScript package
identity. `doctor --fix` materializes immutable SDK-provided package bytes under
the ignored `.vellum/` directory. Project creation materializes the exact UI
package without requiring external npm.

When created by a web or native SDK, one advertised target's initial build and
smoke scenario have already passed. SDKs without that capability report
`capability_unavailable`; that is an error, not a successful no-op.
